  "grammar_explanations": [
    {
      "slug": "present continuous: affirmative for current actions (review)",
      "title_form": "Presente continuo: afirmativo para acciones actuales (repaso)",
      "title_target": "Present Continuous: Affirmative for Current Actions (Review)",
      "description_md_form": "Usamos el **presente continuo** para hablar de acciones que están pasando **ahora mismo**, en este momento. Es como decir \"estoy haciendo\" en español.\n\nLa estructura es muy simple: **sujeto + verbo *to be* (am/is/are) + verbo con -ing**.\n\n- **I am** looking for a product. = Estoy buscando un producto.\n- **She is** picking up the shoes. = Ella está recogiendo los zapatos.\n- **We are** looking for a gift. = Estamos buscando un regalo.\n\nEl verbo *to be* cambia según la persona: *am* para *I*, *is* para *he/she/it*, y *are* para *you/we/they*. El verbo principal siempre termina en **-ing**.\n\nEn esta lección lo usamos mucho con **look for** (buscar) y **pick up** (recoger), porque describen lo que hacemos en una tienda en el momento de hablar.",
      "description_md_target": "We use the **present continuous** to talk about actions happening **right now**, at this moment. It is like saying \"estoy haciendo\" in Spanish.\n\nThe structure is very simple: **subject + verb *to be* (am/is/are) + verb with -ing**.\n\n- **I am** looking for a product. = Estoy buscando un producto.\n- **She is** picking up the shoes. = Ella está recogiendo los zapatos.\n- **We are** looking for a gift. = Estamos buscando un regalo.\n\nThe verb *to be* changes with the person: *am* for *I*, *is* for *he/she/it*, and *are* for *you/we/they*. The main verb always ends in **-ing**.\n\nIn this lesson we use it a lot with **look for** and **pick up**, because they describe what we do in a store at the moment of speaking.",
      "grammar_structure": "Subject + to be (am/is/are) + verb-ing + complement",
      "conjugation_table": {
        "name": "present_continuous_affirmative",
        "headers": [
          "Pronombre",
          "To be",
          "Verbo -ing",
          "Ejemplo"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "I",
            "am",
            "looking",
            "I am looking for a product."
          ],
          [
            "You",
            "are",
            "picking up",
            "You are picking up the shoes."
          ],
          [
            "He/She/It",
            "is",
            "looking",
            "She is looking for a gift."
          ],
          [
            "We",
            "are",
            "looking",
            "We are looking for a pair of shoes."
          ],
          [
            "They",
            "are",
            "picking up",
            "They are picking up the product."
          ]
        ]
      },
